														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3687015">
									

<ul>
<li>They aren't - but they have to be <em>very</em> insistent about it, because the alternative is that they've been needlessly torturing genuine copies of valued employees.</li>
<li>There are like three million test logs that couldn't make it in because they were bloating the article. I tried to reference them in a few places but didn't get much farther than that. The Samothrace thing alludes to the fact that cognitohazards don't 'stick' from one replica to the next, which means there isn't a 'host consciousness' responsible for the replicas - at least not in the traditional sense of a consciousness. The comment about electrical testing alludes to the fact that they've built up a fairly comprehensive model of how currents/data pass through this thing, and that's what led them to the suspicion that old replicas aren't deleted when a new one is created. Ultimately, though, none of that made it into the article, which means they're relegated to my headcanons rather than actual canon.</li>
</ul>

							</div>

								
